    <briefdescription>
<para>RAII wrapper around FLINT&apos;s <computeroutput>fmpq_mat_t</computeroutput> for translating dense <computeroutput><ref refid="ringelem_8hpp_a845589cbe81fb92f0ca26c8b911f8f38_1a845589cbe81fb92f0ca26c8b911f8f38" kindref="member">QQ</ref></computeroutput>-coefficient matrices between the engine and FLINT. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Rational counterpart of <computeroutput><ref refid="class_flint_z_z_mat" kindref="compound">FlintZZMat</ref></computeroutput>: bridges <computeroutput><ref refid="class_d_mat" kindref="compound">DMat</ref>&lt;<ref refid="namespace_m2_a4020664aefa28984a9e3e19b16a31981_1a4020664aefa28984a9e3e19b16a31981" kindref="member">M2::ARingQQ</ref>&gt;</computeroutput> (GMP-backed) and FLINT&apos;s <computeroutput>fmpq_mat_t</computeroutput> via entrywise translation, frees the FLINT matrix in the destructor, and exposes <computeroutput><ref refid="class_flint_q_q_mat_a3a263e83042fdcd86c4def0fe7ca3cee_1a3a263e83042fdcd86c4def0fe7ca3cee" kindref="member">value()</ref></computeroutput> so callers can hand the underlying <computeroutput>fmpq_mat_struct*</computeroutput> straight to FLINT&apos;s matrix routines. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
